    "created_at": "2020-06-30T21:29:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-30T21:29:31Z",
    "body": "Yes I agree. In terms of tests, my work [added tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/14899) about the ordering between style sheet load/error event & scripting and removing / loading style sheets. I think there are still two kinds of tests needed:\r\n - CSS subresources / their relationship to the load-blocking behavior (though it sounds like this still needs to be resolved)\r\n    - https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/5525\r\n - How `text/css`, resource type, and quirks mode affect the load/error event\r\n    - https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/10350\r\n\r\nAlso regarding the first comment's test case, I think we can write tests for the HTTP case, since Fetch returns a network error for requests blocked by mixed content. For the HTTPs case, I guess that'd be covered by the tests in the second bullet above?",
